{"id":770,"name":"palossand","speciesId":770,"dex":770,"form":"normal","generation":7,"types":["ghost","ground"],"stats":{"hp":85,"attack":75,"defense":110,"special-attack":100,"special-defense":75,"speed":35},"abilities":[{"name":"water-compaction","hidden":false},{"name":"sand-veil","hidden":true}],"height":13,"weight":2500,"baseExp":168,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/770.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/770.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/770.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/770.ogg","genus":"Sand Castle Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon do Castelo de Areia","flavor":[{"version":"sun","text":"Possessed people controlled by this Pokémon transformed its sand mound into a castle. As it evolved, its power to curse grew ever stronger."},{"version":"moon","text":"Buried beneath the castle are masses of dried-up bones from those whose vitality it has drained."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"Each of its grains of sand has its own will. Palossand eats small Pokémon and siphons away their vital essence while they’re still alive."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"Once it has whipped up a sandstorm to halt its opponents in their tracks, this terrifying Pokémon snatches away their vitality."},{"version":"sword","text":"Palossand is known as the Beach Nightmare. It pulls its prey down into the sand by controlling the sand itself, and then it sucks out their souls."},{"version":"shield","text":"This Pokémon lives on beaches, but it hates water. Palossand can’t maintain its castle-like shape if it gets drenched by a heavy rain."}],"flavorPt":"Este Pokémon vive nas praias, mas odeia água. Palossand não consegue manter a forma de castelo se for encharcado por uma chuva forte.","genderRate":4,"captureRate":60,"eggG